"Taipei MarketBeat | CN | Cushman & Wakefield (https://www.cushmanwakefield.com/en/greater-china/insights/marketbeats/taipei-marketbeat)\nciteturn156search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: today; Cushman & Wakefield MarketBeat reports analyze quarterly economic and commercial real estate activity including supply, demand and pricing trends at the market and submarket levels. ...   * Taipei Retail MarketBeat Q2 2026\n\n# Taipei MarketBeat Reports\n\n##### Eason Lee • 14/10/2026\n\nCushman & Wakefield MarketBeat reports analyze quarterly economic and commercial real estate activity including supply, demand and pricing trends at the market and submarket levels.\n\n### Q3 2026 Highlights\n\nOffice: New Grade A office supply remained paused in Q3.\n\nRetail: General merchandise retail sales rose 6.0% y-o-y in the first eight months of 2026.\n\nIndustrial Office: Large-scale leasing transactions reduced vacancy across NHTP in Q3.\n\nCapital Markets: Quarterly transaction volume reached a record NT$105.8 billion in Q3.\n\nLearn more by clicking our most recent Taipei MarketBeat reports below.\n\n## CURRENT MARKETBEATS\n\n##### Taipei Office MarketBeat\n\n* * *\n\nNew Grade A office supply remained paused in Q3. Corporate relocations lifted the citywide vacancy rate slightly to 7.3%, while year-to-date net absorption reached approximately 15,000 pings. Average rents remained stable at NT$2,860 per ping per month, with limited rental movement across submarkets. Ahead, two new projects scheduled for completion in Q4 will add 27,100 pings of space.\n\n \n\nClick here to download the report\n\n##### Taipei Industrial Office MarketBeat\n\n* * *\n\nLarge-scale leasing transactions reduced vacancy across NHTP in Q3, with the overall vacancy rate dropping from 11.1% to 10.3%. Vacancy fell in the Xihu, Wende and Jiuzong sections, supported by occupier expansions and relocations. Average rents remained stable across the park, although performance continued to diverge between newer and older buildings, while capital values were broadly unchanged.\n\nClick here to download the report\n\n##### Taipei Retail MarketBeat\n\n* * *\n\nGeneral merchandise retail sales rose 6.0% y-o-y in the first eight months of 2026, supported by summer spending, seasonal purchases and new mall openings. Vacancy rates across the key retail districts remained broadly stable, reflecting steady leasing demand. Garden City’s new Monet Garden retail area highlights the integration of shopping, entertainment and sports-related consumption.\n\nClick here to download the report\n\n##### Taipei Capital Markets MarketBeat\n\n* * *\n\nQuarterly transaction volume reached a record NT$105.8 billion in Q3, driven by technology sector expansion, with owner-occupier acquisitions accounting for 70% of volume. Industrial assets predominated, although the acquisition of Ruentex Yucheng Plaza highlighted renewed office investment demand. In contrast, land transaction volume totaled NT$25.6 billion, near a three-year low as developers remained cautious.\n\nClick here to download the report\n\n#### Download Previous Office Reports\n\nClick on the title to begin download:\n\n  * Taipei Office MarketBeat Q2 2026\n  * Taipei Office MarketBeat Q1 2026\n  * Taipei Office MarketBeat Q4 2025\n\n#### Download Previous Industrial Reports\n\nClick on the title to begin download:\n\n  * Taipei Industrial MarketBeat Q2 2026\n  * Taipei Industrial MarketBeat Q1 2026\n  * Taipei Industrial MarketBeat Q4 2025\n\n#### Download Previous Retail Reports\n\nClick on the title to begin download:\n\n  * Taipei Retail MarketBeat Q2 2026\n  * Taipei Retail MarketBeat Q1 2026\n  * Taipei Retail MarketBeat Q4 2025\n\n#### Download Previous Capital Markets Reports\n\nClick on the title to begin download:\n\n  * Taipei Capital Markets MarketBeat Q2 2026\n  * Taipei Capital Markets MarketBeat Q1 2026\n  * Taipei Capital Markets MarketBeat Q4 2025-------------------------------------------------------